---
title: Gyudon
servings: 1
course: dinner
cuisine: Japanese
tags: quick, beef, egg, simmered, rice
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Bring water to a boil in a #saucepan{} covered with a #lid{}. Gently lower in the @egg{1} and boil for ~{6%minutes}. Once cooked, transfer to cold water to shock, then peel under water and set aside.

In a second #saucepan{}, add @water{100%ml} and bring toward a simmer. Stir in the @dashi powder{1%packet}, followed by @mirin{2%tbsp}, @sake{2%tbsp}, and @soy sauce{2%tbsp}.

Using a #grater{}, finely grate the @garlic{1%clove} and @ginger{10%g} directly into the broth. Turn the heat down to low so the liquid gently simmers.

Thinly slice the @brown onion{1} and add it all into the simmering broth. Let cook until the onions are completely soft and translucent.

While the onions cook, thinly slice the @beef steak{200%g} against the grain. Finely slice the @spring onion{2}, reserving some of the dark green slices for garnish.

Once the onions are soft, add the sliced beef to the saucepan. Stir with a #spatula{} to gently poach the meat in the simmering liquid until cooked through without boiling aggressively. If the liquid reduces too much, add a splash of @water{30%ml}. Taste and adjust with a pinch of @salt{1%pinch} if needed.

Turn off the heat, add most of the sliced spring onions, and stir through the hot beef and broth.

Add warm cooked @cooked rice{1%serving} to a serving #bowl{}. Pour the beef, onions, and broth over the rice. Garnish with the peeled soft-boiled @&egg{}, @pickled ginger{1%tbsp}, the reserved @&spring onion{}, and a sprinkle of @sesame seed{1%tsp}.
